{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion lag: The model consistently underestimates immediate post-dip recoveries (e.g., Dec 13-15) and overestimates post-peak declines, failing to capture the sharp V-shaped volatility in the first 5-10 days of the forecast horizon.",
    "Apply aggressive downward adjustment after upward spikes: When history shows a rapid price increase (e.g., Dec 21, May 20), the model's linear upward drift significantly overshoots the subsequent peak, requiring a manual reduction of 3-5 EUR in the first 5 days to align with the inevitable correction.",
    "Ignore low-magnitude sentiment signals: Sentiment values of 0.20 or 0.33 do not correlate with sustained trend changes; treat them as noise and rely primarily on price momentum rather than sentiment-driven adjustments.",
    "Adjust for long-term decay bias: The model projects a slow, steady increase or flatline over the 30-day horizon, whereas true outcomes exhibit a distinct downward drift after the initial volatility; apply a negative slope correction for days 15-30.",
    "Cap forecast peaks: The model fails to anticipate the magnitude of the peak (e.g., hitting ~80 EUR in Dec) before the drop; reduce the forecasted peak value by approximately 2-3 EUR to match the actual market ceiling."
  ]
}
